.TH "fi_mon_sampler" "1" "2026\-10\-22" "Libfabric Programmer\(cqs Manual" "#VERSION#"
.SH NAME
fi_mon_sampler \- Simple sampler for ofi_hook_monitor provider.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
 fi_mon_sampler [OPTIONS] <target>      sample from file(s) at <target>
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Extract data from the ofi_hook_monitor provider via communication files.
\f[CR]<target>\f[R] can either be one communication file or a folder of
files.
Data is exported based on \f[CR]\-f <format>\f[R] and either printed to
stdout (only for single files), or stored per communication file at
\f[CR]\-o <outpath>\f[R].
The sampler can watch the communication files for changes via the option
\f[CR]\-w <msec>\f[R] for repeated sampling.
.PP
The name format of the output files is based on the ofi_hook_monitor
provider and is as follows:
\f[CR]<ppid>_<pid>_<sequential id>_<job id>_<provider name>\f[R].
\f[CR]ppid\f[R] and \f[CR]pid\f[R] are taken from the perspective of the
monitored application.
In a batched environment running SLURM, \f[CR]job id\f[R] is set to the
SLURM job ID, otherwise it is set to 0.
.SH HOW TO RUN
Launch a libfabric application with \f[CR]FI_HOOK=monitor\f[R] to enable
the ofi_hook_monitor provider.
Adjust the monitor provider settings according to \f[CR]fi_hook\f[R](7).
.PP
Then launch the sampler via
\f[CR]fi_mon_sampler \-o <output> <target>\f[R].
By default, the ofi_hook_monitor provider stores data at
\f[CR]/dev/shm/ofi/<uid>/<hostname>\f[R].
.PP
The sampler will generate output files in the directory specified at
\f[CR]<output>\f[R], one for each monitored provider.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[I]\-w <msec>\f[R]
Watch files for changes, check every <msec> milliseconds.
.TP
\f[I]\-f <format>\f[R]
Output format.
Currently only supports CSV.
.TP
\f[I]\-o <outpath>\f[R]
Output file path.
Uses stdout if unset.
.SH USAGE EXAMPLES
Launch a libfabric application and enable the ofi_hook_monitor provider:
.IP
.EX
FI_HOOK=monitor fi_pingpong [OPTIONS]
.EE
.PP
Launch another \f[CR]fi_pingpong\f[R] with the respective settings.
.PP
Finally, launch the sampler:
.IP
.EX
fi_mon_sampler \-o $HOME \-w 1000 \-f csv /dev/shm/ofi/$UID/$HOSTNAME
.EE
.SH OUTPUT
Output files will be generated in the folder specified at
\f[CR]\-o <output>\f[R].
.PP
In \f[CR]\-f csv\f[R] mode, this will contain a CSV file with data for
all monitored libfabric functions.
For each function, both the \f[CR]count\f[R] and \f[CR]sum\f[R] counters
are exported, indicated by the column name suffix \f[CR]_c\f[R] and
\f[CR]_s\f[R] respectively.
In addition, each function is monitored for each data size bucket.
Refer to \f[CR]fi_hook\f[R](7) for more details.
.PP
Example CSV output, first four columns, first three rows:
.IP
.EX
mon_recv_0_64_c,mon_recv_0_64_s,mon_recv_64_512_c,mon_recv_64_512_s
0,0,0,0
22529,0,0,0
113664,0,0,0
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
\f[CR]fi_hook\f[R](7)
